RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE

Office of City Clerk

March 10, 2017

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date beginning
at 6:05 p.m. in City Council Chambers for the purpose of collective labor bargaining with the Cheyenne
Professional Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local No. 279.  Present were:
MAYOR - Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS – Bryan Cook, Richard Johnson, Pete Laybourn, Scott
Roybal, Dicky Shanor and Jeff White.  Absent: Rocky Case, Mike Luna and Dr. Mark Rinne.  Also present
were:  Kylie Soden, Deputy City Clerk; Sylvia Hackl, City Attorney; Alessandra McCoy, Assistant City
Attorney, Lois Huff, City Treasurer, and Tom Schingle, Interim Chief, Fire and Rescue Department.  The
pledge of allegiance was recited.

Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded, and stated that Wyoming State Statute
§16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings Act allows the governing body to meet in executive session to
consider or tender offers regarding wages, salaries, or other terms and conditions of employment during
negotiations with the fire fighters union and that any motion approved by the governing body to move
into executive session during the special meetings would be pursuant to this section of statute.  Mayor Orr
further advised if the governing body met in executive session, they would be meeting in the City Council
Administrative office, and that Fire Union representatives were welcome to use Room 104 for the purpose
of meeting to caucus.  She stated that spokespersons for the City are herself and Dicky Shanor, and
Jonathan Bertsch and Andrew Dykeshorn are the spokespersons for the Union.  She noted that any
collective labor agreement that may be reached must be approved by the governing body with the
agreement placed on the City Council agenda for approval.

Relative to one of the City’s previously stated priorities, Mayor Orr inquired whether the Union
has any solutions to manage overtime costs.  Mr. Bertsch advised there currently aren’t many options
without restructuring the organization.  He explained the Union has been conducting research and is
hopeful that the new proposed Labor/Management Relations section of the contract, which provides for
regular meetings between the administration and Union representatives, will help in this area.  Mr. Shanor
moved to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all
members of the governing body present.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped;
executive session convened at 6:13 p.m. in the City Council Administrative office]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 6:57 p.m.
Mr. Shanor presented the City’s counteroffer on the following sections, or portions thereof:  Section 22,
Classification of Employment and Basic Wages; Section 23, Overtime, and Section 29, Sick Leave.
Mayor Orr recessed the meeting at 7:01 p.m. to allow Union representatives to caucus.  [City Clerk note:
Audio recording of the meeting was stopped]

Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 7:07 p.m.  Mr. Bertsch provided further information
on overtime cost concerns and steps that can be taken to minimize overtime, explaining that major
contributing factors to overtime are unpredictable sick leave and employee turnover.  Mr. Bertsch
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
presented and discussed the Union’s counteroffers on the following sections, or portions thereof: Section
22, Classification of Employment and Basic Wages; Section 23, Overtime, and Section 29, Sick Leave.
Upon inquiry, Mr. Bertsch and Mr. Dykeshorn explained the Union’s overtime algorithm.  Mr. Shanor
moved to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Johnson.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all
members of the governing body present.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped;
executive session convened at 7:26 p.m. in the City Council Administrative office]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 7:39 p.m.
Mayor Orr expressed that the City recognizes that a priority of the Union is retaining benefits.  Mr. Shanor
presented the City’s counteroffer on the following section: Section 22, Classification of Employment and
Basic Wages.  It was noted the City has no objections to proposed Sections 23, Overtime, and 29, Sick
Leave.  Mayor Orr recessed the meeting at 7:41 p.m. to allow Union representatives to caucus.  [City
Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped]

Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 7:52 p.m.  Mr. Bertsch presented and discussed the
Union’s counteroffer on Section 22, Classification of Employment and Basic Wages. Mr. Shanor moved
to meet in executive session, seconded by Mr. Cook.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” -- all members of the
governing body present.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped; executive session
convened at 7:59 p.m. in the City Council Administrative office]

Following closure of the executive session, Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 8:21 p.m.
She provided information on the City’s financial outlook and advised she has asked all City departments
to present a level budget for the upcoming fiscal year.  She commented on items within the proposed
contract that will be of benefit to fire fighters, and presented the City’s counteroffer on Section 22,
Classification of Employment and Basic Wages.  Mayor Orr recessed the meeting at 8:24 p.m. to allow
Union representatives to caucus.  [City Clerk note: Audio recording of the meeting was stopped]

Mayor Orr reconvened the special meeting at 8:51 p.m.  Mr. Bertsch presented and discussed the
Union’s counteroffers on the following sections, or portions thereof: Section 27, Wellness/Fitness
Program; Section 33, Uniforms, and Section 22, Classification of Employment and Basic Wages.

Mayor Orr stated the next special meeting would be held on March 14, 2017.  She stated the
purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no other business previously noted for the
special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 8:56 p.m.

Submitted by,

Kylie Soden

Deputy City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.

Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

March 27, 2017
```
